#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:5
#: 1e243fd939104d339824d234b6a4120a
msgid "DroneCAN Adapter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:7
#: 65986681cc8c4267a8755fcac2cd3f52
msgid "These are several ways that a DroneCAN adapter node running AP_Periph can be used and this page is a small selection of the possibilities. These sections should walk you through setting up the autopilot and the node so that they work together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:9
#: 16af64ae1cc34735942ef9b247afeb88
msgid "DroneCAN Adapter nodes usually come with firmware that supports a subset of ArduPilot's large peripheral capability. Be sure to check that the firmware supplied supports the peripherals you are attemptime to setup. If not, check the `Firmware <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph/>`__  page for possible alternative firmware for that adapter that may have the capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:12
#: 16b1957521c148b5a5a9d015c8eefc4d
msgid "GPS Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:13
#: c595d2bb3e35483e8f02b85fe1a06cbe
msgid "Attach the GPS to a DroneCAN Adapter's serial port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:15
#: 3cfcd8c4615849f1afb8601ceb8c0ab5
msgid "set :ref:`GPS1_TYPE<GPS1_TYPE>` = 9 on the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:16
#: d93e8d542d574f8ea441fcea3a90cd4c
msgid "set the DroneCAN adapter's ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` on which the GPS is connected to 5 (GPS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:19
#: b6b50a3ca3a74a3baf90a599c0253e96
msgid "Compass Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:20
#: 4397bae7782b4abeb2e0564918768c88
msgid "Attach the Compass to the DroneCAN Adapter's external I2C port. It will appear as a normal Compass in ArduPilot and normal :ref:`compass setup procedures<common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>` would apply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:22
#: 12b24c24ce3045b482987bbe6d2db074
msgid "The MatekL431 CAN Adapter comes setup for a SPI connected Compass (RM3100). If an I2C Compass is attached, different firmware must be loaded for it to function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:25
#: 1a71130aa54f43549cddc2a078655dbd
msgid "I2C Airspeed Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:26
#: 20adb0660d6c45398f1680e06d609611
msgid "Attach to the I2C bus pinned out from the DroneCAN Adapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:28
#: f9313dc9c1b1430580c8fe307b02c2fe
msgid "set :ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>` =8 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:29
#: db40be5e86ce4698a2b57c29934da93a
msgid "set the DroneCAN's ``ARSPD_TYPE`` parameter to match the type of airspeed sensor connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:32
#: 144dd3b031e7456fb4bd1f8bbf0d46d2
msgid "Rangefinder Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:33
#: 9693ef6361a246659c582c66d1260ff4
msgid "To use rangefinders, follow the instructions at  :ref:`DroneCAN Setup Advanced<common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` to set up the ArduPilot parameters. Using MissionPlanner or DroneCAN Gui, set the parameters on the adaptor node following the instructions for the relevant rangefinder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:35
#: a79fdc2e2f9e44d6b1414108184f4ff1
msgid "The orientation of the rangefinder (RNGFND1_ORIENT) must be set to 0 on the adaptor node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:37
#: ced91e6b4b564fd4b5f221bece1f94b9
msgid "The RNGFNDx_ADDR ArduPilot parameter must be set above 0 and be equal to the number set on the DroneCAN adapter node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:40
#: b8f7706a35c84cdcb370c8b05b76d5e2
msgid "PWM or DShot Output Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:41
#: 9d978c9fb90b42158ed942eb05c93dda
msgid "Adapters that have timer outputs available can be used as PWM and DShot output nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:43
#: a917e18b8e2e494a96508261191115bc
msgid "The `MatekL431 DroneCAN PWM device <https://www.mateksys.com/?portfolio=can-l4-pwm>`__ is an example of this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:45
#: e6fcc1ce22514d4eb512c7b9c85e2674
msgid "This can be useful for providing additional servo outputs beyond what the autopilot provides, but is most useful for allowing the ESCs and Sevos to be remotely located, far from the autopilot using the CAN bus to communicate. A maximum of 32 outputs in ArduPilot is possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:47
#: 3bd4d95ce2e643caa567b9df0fadc7c4
msgid "In addition, the autopilot outputs can be configured for GPIO use, and still allow up to 32 servo/motor outputs to be realized with DroneCAN peripherals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:49
#: a6d152501c9249e687e5016887b651b8
msgid "In order to use DShot output, the node must have a DShot-capable firmware installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:52
#: e5b0479e2e124c69b09738b7c68b7b11
msgid "DShot ESC Adapter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:53
#: 98e50bc3aea54a979fcb87782d9139d1
msgid "In this example, a quadplane with outputs 5-8 used for 4 DShot ESCs with telemetry will be shown. 3 wires from each ESC should be connected to the DroneCAN adapter node: Ground, DShot signal, and serial telemetry. The ground from each ESC should be connected to a ground pad on the DroneCAN node. The signal wires from the 4 ESCs should be connected to the first 4 PWM pads on the node, marked as outputs “1”, “2”, “3”, and “4”. The serial telemetry pin from all 4 ESCs should be all connected to the same UART RX pin on the adapter node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:55
#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:69
#: 2cc200e3c73041a182dd2be424b00ccd
#: 1c6f7d5668744a8bb858beb904e14b32
msgid "On the main autopilot you need to set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:57
#: d83160fcf8324f75b21af325810f6293
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Px_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:58
#: d755d876263148c2be9864ab5359dde3
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Dx_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:59
#: f5c29fc5ef8f40b29595bd1b8741b611
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Dx_UC_ESC_BM <CAN_D1_UC_ESC_BM>` = 240 or the bitmask of motor outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:60
#: c75e3213aad94da19ebdac00368c2b3e
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Dx_UC_ESC_OF <CAN_D1_UC_ESC_OF>` = 4 or the offset number to the first ESC output. This makes the transmission of CAN packets much more efficient"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:62
#: 806b5672951f42588f3df2a6e8590cbd
msgid "On the DroneCAN PWM node you need to set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:64
#: f2e073c40199492088745e22346d7679
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_FUNCTION <dev:OUT1_FUNCTION>` = 33 + ESC number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:65
#: 91e60d999fb84139bbf6ba6615797f10
msgid ":ref:`OUT_BLH_MASK <dev:OUT_BLH_MASK>` = 15 or a bitmask of which ESCs are active"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:68
#: 8e2463ead38e4a42a992f3cb62aef9e4
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:71
#: 57ee1981c1cc4b8b99c50bcd50027d88
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Dx_UC_SRV_BM <CAN_D1_UC_SRV_BM>` to a bitmask of servos you want to send over CAN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:72
#: 992a61953c2541999f09d213ed7611f7
msgid ":ref:`CAN_Dx_UC_SRV_RT <CAN_D1_UC_SRV_RT>` to the output rate. This is typically 50 Hz for most servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:74
#: 0ce48106572048ffa649c348d418bd45
msgid "On the CAN node you need to set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:76
#: 7932574ad9e44c7da32aff1c52088e63
msgid ":ref:`OUT_BLH_MASK <dev:OUT_BLH_MASK>` = 0 to disable DShot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:77
#: d1286e68beee407490297e47740a629e
msgid ":ref:`ESC_PWM_TYPE <dev:ESC_PWM_TYPE>` = 0 for normal PWM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:78
#: e9dfec78e9a64a4ebafeb83b815f32bb
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_FUNCTION <dev:OUT1_FUNCTION>` to a value of 50 plus the servo number for each output you want to be enabled as PWM output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:79
#: bfd7b9d7cb8e457886ca0fae50901966
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_FUNCTION <dev:OUT1_FUNCTION>` = 0 for any outputs you do not have connected. Do not leave them at the default of 33 + ESC number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:81
#: ce0effab2af94a2a965f5f31e625e9d0
msgid "For example, if you had an elevator servo on SERVO2 on the main autopilot and you want this to appear on the first output of the CAN node (on the node's pin marked “1”) then you would set OUT1_FUNCTION = 52 (that is 50 + the servo number on the autopilot). If you wanted a rudder that is on SERVO4 to appear on output 4 then you would set OUT4_FUNCTION=54."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:83
#: 9145374b5b5d46a78e2f16b0e95361ed
msgid "It is also recommended to set OUTn_MIN to 1000, OUTn_MAX to 2000, and OUTn_TRIM to 1500. That will allow you to use the SERVOn_MIN, SERVOn_MAX, and SERVOn_TRIM values on the main autopilot to control the outputs range and center in the usual way. It is possible to use other values on the node, but it gets more complicated to understand the mapping of the PWM values, so using 1000, 1500, 2000 is recommended. Doing this also means the PWM value in your autopilot logs matches what is output by the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:86
#: c3ad2ac4ef49414f9a16178eafc9b9f6
msgid "Combining DShot and PWM outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ap-periph-usage-examples.rst:87
#: cb002c246ec841e6b694ee7b4ddce04d
msgid "There are a few rules to follow when combining PWM and DShot outputs on the same node. If you are familiar with doing this on autopilot, it is the same rules. The pins are grouped by timer and all of the pins attached to a timer must be the same type. For example, on the MatekL431 node the first 4 outputs are all on the same timer. This means that those output pins must all be DShot outputs and 1 PWM on the fifth output or the first 4 as PWM and 1 DShot."
msgstr ""
